From 15ea5f1898671300c06cf68b5f42bf9c6c8a2d40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gugu-acp <gugu-acp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 04:38:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Serve ACP v2 with independent foreground work and task
 control

Why: a completed parent prompt must admit the next input while its native
children continue to stream and request permissions. Remove v1 wire routing,
deferred parent settlement, obsolete cancellation wrappers and held-turn tests.
Expose steering (including next delivery) and async-task stop as named v2
extensions; preserve standard v2 child associations even for AIR-marked clients.

Upstream: foreground settlement, child permission ownership, v2 steering,
independent task control and delegation metadata can be proposed separately.
The v2-only wire policy and removal of v1 tests are Gugu release policy, not
requirements for upstream consumers that still support v1.
Drop: when upstream v2 serves equivalent steering/task control, independent
parent completion and child permission ownership; retain only the v2 entry policy.
