+### ACP v2
 
-Without either signal, Agent and Task stay ordinary tool calls and child interactions stay on the
-root session. Clients that use the historical `_meta["subagent-transcript"]` capability or the
-`forwardSubagentText` session option retain the flattened child transcript.
+This build serves [draft ACP v2](https://agentclientprotocol.com/protocol/v2/overview)
+only. There is no environment switch or v1 router. A v1 initialization is rejected.
+The internal agent reuses upstream's typed conversion helpers; its foreground work
+ends at the parent result even while independently running children remain live.
 
-### Experimental ACP v2
+`session/prompt` returns an admission receipt (`messageId`). Foreground completion,
+usage and errors arrive through `state_update`. Child output, child completion and
+permission requests continue after parent idle. Subagents always use the standard
+v2 `subagent_update` shape, including when a client sends older extension markers.
+Association metadata `delegationToolCallId` identifies the real launch tool call.
 
-Started with `CLAUDE_AGENT_ACP_EXPERIMENTAL_V2=1`, the adapter also serves the
-[draft ACP v2](https://agentclientprotocol.com/protocol/v2/overview): a client that asks for
-protocol version 2 or later in `initialize` gets v2, and every other client gets v1, as before.
-The draft can still change, and this surface changes with it.
+Named extensions:
 
-On v2 the adapter serves the session baseline (`session/new`, `session/list`, `session/resume`
-with replay, `session/close`, `session/prompt`, `session/cancel`), `session/delete`,
-`session/fork`, additional directories, config options (the mode is one), plans, notices,
-compaction, display terminals for commands, permission requests, elicitation, providers, auth, and
-[subagents](#subagent-sessions). Steering and the AIR extensions are v1 only for now.
+- `_session/steering`: inject into active foreground work. `_meta.steering.delivery:
+"next"` waits for the current tool boundary. `idleBehavior: "promptRequired"`
+  leaves an idle request with its host for normal `session/prompt` submission.
+- `_session/async_task/update`: independently running command/workflow updates,
+  enabled by `capabilities._meta.asyncTasks: true`.
+- `_session/async_task/stop`: stop exactly one advertised background task.
+- Individual child cancellation uses standard `session/cancel` with the child id.
+
+The session baseline, resume/replay, fork, config options, plans, notices,
+compaction, display terminals, permissions, elicitation, providers and auth use
+upstream v2's surface. The draft can still change.
 
